{"created": "2026-07-14T12:33:11.903287+00:00", "modified": "2026-07-14T12:33:17.326913+00:00", "id": 21358203, "conceptrecid": "21353208", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21358203", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21353208", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21358203", "metadata": {"title": "Preliminary Numerical Study of Gray-Cat Metastable Interfaces, Weak C Readout, and Strong D Observation Selection in a Closed Phase System", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21358203", "publication_date": "2026-07-14", "description": "This preliminary numerical study models white-cat and black-cat alternatives as internal A/B allocation amplitudes in a closed complex phase system. It distinguishes a gray-cat eigen phase, a gray-cat metastable phase, natural selection, and large oscillation regimes. It then tests weak C readout windows and strong D observation selection while comparing against no-D controls. The study shows that weak readout can preserve and read a metastable gray allocation, while stronger observation can select a white or black allocation; gray eigen states remain gray even under strong observation.", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kihara, Noriaki", "affiliation": "WF System Co., Ltd.", "orcid": "0009-0004-6753-4020"}], "keywords": ["closed phase system", "Schrodinger cat", "metastable state", "weak readout", "measurement selection", "complex amplitude", "numerical experiment"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21315735", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21333766", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "v2", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "21353208"}}]}}, "title": "Preliminary Numeric